    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "datasource",
        "uid": "-- Grafana --"
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Catalyst \u00b7 Relay & Container Runtime \u2014 WHERE work runs, and is it attributed?\nThe mini execution-core daemons are **retired**. Work runs as **laptop relay workers** (`relay-dispatch.sh`, one `claude -p` per ticket) and, next, as **Cloudflare container runners**.\n\n**Per-ticket economics already exist \u2014 use [Claude Code \u2014 Unified](/d/claude-code-unified) for those.** Its *Token Burn by Ticket*, *Cost by Ticket*, *Cost by Phase* and *Attribution Health* panels are keyed on `linear_key` / `task_type`, which relay workers now stamp, so they light up with no change. This dashboard covers only what those panels do **not**: which runtime the work ran on, and whether relay attribution is landing.\n\n**Discriminators** (all verified live): relay workers set `catalyst_orchestration=\"relay\"`; container runners additionally set the semconv `cloud_platform` / `container_id` / `service_instance_id` (verified end-to-end through the CF tunnel \u2014 an OTLP post carrying them arrived in Loki with every attribute promoted).\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Relay attribution reaches Claude Code only via `claude --settings <file>` \u2014 a plain `env VAR=\u2026 claude` is overridden by `~/.claude/settings.json`'s own `env` block. If *Relay attribution health* below reads 0%, that is the first thing to check."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Is relay attribution landing?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Relay attribution",
      "description": "Share of live relay series that carry a linear_key. Should be 1. Zero means --settings is not reaching the worker (see the note above); the denominator is clamped so an idle relay reads 'no data', not a divide-by-zero.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "count(claude_code_token_usage_tokens_total{catalyst_orchestration=\"relay\",linear_key!=\"\"}) / clamp_min(count(claude_code_token_usage_tokens_total{catalyst_orchestration=\"relay\"}), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Relay attribution",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#73BF69",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "noValue": "no data",
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background_solid",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "values": false,
          "fields": ""
        }
      }
    },
